    "result_text": "All tests pass. The change is complete and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented soft-delete for owners across the Spring Boot stack:\n\n**Domain model** (`Owner.java`)\n- Added a persistent `deleted` boolean field (`@Column(name = \"deleted\")`) with `isDeleted()`/`setDeleted()`. It defaults to `false`, so a newly created owner is not deleted.\n\n**Service** (`ClinicServiceImpl.java`)\n- `deleteOwner` now flags the owner `deleted = true` and `save`s it (retaining the row) instead of removing it.\n- `assertIdentityUnique` and `assertHouseholdUnique` (the create endpoint's identity/duplicate checks) now skip owners flagged `deleted`, so a duplicate that would normally be blocked is allowed when the only matching owner has been soft-deleted.\n\n**API contract** (`openapi.yml`)\n- Added a read-only `deleted` boolean property to the `Owner` response schema, so `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns it (and MapStruct's generated mapper populates it from the entity). The existing `DELETE` endpoint already returns `204` (2xx).\n\n**Persistence schema** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,postgres,mysql}/schema.sql`)\n- Added a `deleted BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE` column to the `owners` table (ddl-auto is `none`, so the schema is authoritative).\n\n**JDBC repository** (`JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl.java`)\n- Included `deleted` in the owner SELECTs and the UPDATE, so the soft-delete works under the `jdbc` profile too (the tests run under `spring-data-jpa`).\n\nThe acceptance tests \u2014 `coreSoftDeleteFlagsAndRetains` (delete then GET shows `deleted: true`, retained) and `coreDeletedOwnerIgnoredByDuplicateCheck` (re-create allowed after soft-delete) \u2014 both pass, and `BUILD SUCCESS` for the full suite.",
